# ESP32 Capability Test

Three LEDs run a timed sequence controlled by a phone or computer over USB serial at 115200 baud. Intensity levels 1–5 use 5 kHz, 8-bit PWM (duty values 51–255).

## Pins and circuit

| LED | GPIO | Turns on | Turns off |
|---|---|---|---|
| A | 16 | Immediately | 2000 ms |
| B | 17 | 400 ms | 2000 ms |
| C | 18 | 900 ms | 2000 ms |

All times are measured from the same sequence start.

The board checks the simulated input every 200 ms. A value of 2500 or higher turns all outputs off. START is rejected while running or while the input is unsafe. Lowering the value does not restart the sequence; send START again.

To demonstrate safety, start with 1000, run the sequence, then set 3000 while the LEDs are on. The board performs the cutoff without a STOP command. Disconnecting does not send STOP; board timing and safety checks continue.

See `DEVELOPMENT_NOTE.txt` for the short written reflection.
